<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arjuna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arjuna is a hero of the Indian epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, the third of the five Pandava brothers and a peerless archer. His dialogue with his charioteer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> before the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a> forms the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita">Bhagavad Gita</a>. Peoples and kings claimed descent from him, among them the Arjunayanas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, and poets such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adikavi-pampa">Pampa</a> cast their royal patrons in his role.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arjuna.jpg" alt="Arjuna" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ilussion · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arjuna_statue.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
